CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ outer B handler reached: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ outer-try object destroyed during unwinding: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[except.ctor]/1-3, [except.throw]/4 -- an automatic object in an outer scope
that is exited because the exception does not match an inner handler must be
destroyed during unwinding.  Fixed by level-by-level propagation: each try emits
an exceptional-exit landing that runs the destructors of the scopes between it
and the enclosing try, and the exception dispatch routes an unmatched exception
there instead of jumping flat to an outer handler.
